(365, 'How many countries play wheelchair basketball', 'Wheelchair basketball is played in over 100 countries, highlighting its widespread global reach and inclusivity.', '<h1><span style=\"font-size: 14pt;\"><strong>How to Qualify for the Paralympics in Wheelchair Basketball</strong></span></h1>\r\n<p>Qualifying for the Paralympics in wheelchair basketball involves several key steps:</p>\r\n<ol>\r\n<li>\r\n<h2><strong>National Team Selection: <span style=\"font-size: 12pt;\">Athletes must first compete at the national level and be selected for their country&rsquo;s national team. This typically involves participating in domestic competitions and meeting performance standards set by national wheelchair basketball federations.</span></strong></h2>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<h3><strong>International Competitions:</strong> <span style=\"font-size: 12pt;\">Athletes must then compete in international tournaments and events, such as the World Championships and regional qualifiers. Strong performances in these events can help secure a spot in the Paralympic Games.</span></h3>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<h4><strong>Ranking and Qualification Events:</strong> Teams must achieve high rankings in specific qualification tournaments leading up to the Paralympics. The top teams from these events earn spots for their countries in the Games.</h4>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<h5><strong>Compliance with IPC Standards:</strong> Athletes and teams must adhere to the International Paralympic Committee (IPC) standards, including classification guidelines and eligibility criteria.</h5>\r\n</li>\r\n</ol>\r\n<h2><strong>Is Wheelchair Basketball in the Olympics?</strong></h2>\r\n<p>Wheelchair basketball is not part of the Olympic Games. Instead, it is featured in the Paralympic Games, where athletes with disabilities compete at the highest level. The Paralympics, held in parallel with the Olympics, showcase a range of adaptive sports, including wheelchair basketball, which highlights the talents and achievements of athletes with impairments.</p>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n<h3>What are three facts about wheelchair basketball?</h3>\r\n<p>Here are three facts about wheelchair basketball:</p>\r\n<ol>\r\n<li>\r\n<p><strong>International Popularity:</strong> Wheelchair basketball is played in over 100 countries, demonstrating its global reach and inclusivity. It has become a prominent sport in the Paralympic Games and is widely recognized and practiced worldwide.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p><strong>Classification System:</strong> Athletes in wheelchair basketball are classified based on their level of physical impairment to ensure fair competition. The classification system assigns players a point value from 1 to 4.5, with lower scores indicating higher levels of impairment, and teams must adhere to a maximum point limit on the court.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p><strong>Origins and Evolution:</strong> Wheelchair basketball was first developed in the late 1940s by veterans of World War II who were injured and looking for recreational activities. It has since evolved into a highly competitive sport with formal leagues, international competitions, and significant advancements in equipment and training.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ol>\r\n<div class=\"flex-1 overflow-hidden\">\r\n<div class=\"h-full\">\r\n<div class=\"react-scroll-to-bottom--css-qujcf-79elbk h-full\">\r\n<div class=\"react-scroll-to-bottom--css-qujcf-1n7m0yu\">\r\n<div class=\"flex flex-col text-sm md:pb-9\">\r\n<article class=\"w-full text-token-text-primary focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:outline-offset-[-4px]\" dir=\"auto\" data-testid=\"conversation-turn-27\" data-scroll-anchor=\"true\">\r\n<div class=\"text-base py-[18px] px-3 md:px-4 m-auto w-full md:px-5 lg:px-1 xl:px-5\">\r\n<div class=\"mx-auto flex flex-1 gap-4 text-base md:gap-5 lg:gap-6 md:max-w-3xl\">\r\n<div class=\"group/conversation-turn relative flex w-full min-w-0 flex-col agent-turn\">\r\n<div class=\"flex-col gap-1 md:gap-3\">\r\n<div class=\"flex max-w-full flex-col flex-grow\">\r\n<div class=\"min-h-[20px] text-message flex w-full flex-col items-end gap-2 break-words [.text-message+&amp;]:mt-5 overflow-x-auto whitespace-normal\" dir=\"auto\" data-message-author-role=\"assistant\" data-message-id=\"f09ecc46-7e7b-4c10-b65c-a3beec1c936e\">\r\n<div class=\"flex w-full flex-col gap-1 empty:hidden first:pt-[3px]\">\r\n<div class=\"markdown prose w-full break-words dark:prose-invert dark\">\r\n<p><strong>Wheelchair Basketball at the 2024 Paralympics</strong></p>\r\n<p>At the 2024 Paralympic Games, held in Paris, wheelchair basketball will feature prominently as one of the key sports. The competition will showcase elite athletes with disabilities competing at the highest level.</p>\r\n<p><strong>Key Points:</strong></p>\r\n<ol>\r\n<li>\r\n<p><strong>Event Structure:</strong> The wheelchair basketball tournament will include both men\'s and women\'s events, with teams from around the world competing for gold, silver, and bronze medals. The tournament format will involve group stages followed by knockout rounds.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p><strong>Qualification:</strong> Teams from various countries have qualified through regional and international tournaments, adhering to the standards set by the International Wheelchair Basketball Federation (IWBF) and the International Paralympic Committee (IPC).</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p><strong>Highlights:</strong> The 2024 Paralympics will feature top wheelchair basketball teams, with matches broadcast globally and showcasing the sport&rsquo;s high level of skill, strategy, and athleticism.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ol>\r\n<p>For more updates on the wheelchair basketball events and athletes participating in the 2024 Paralympics, visit examinfo.blog</p>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div class=\"mt-3 w-full empty:hidden\">&nbsp;</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div class=\"absolute\">&nbsp;</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</article>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>', '1725010011-wheelchair-basketball_625x300_30_August_24.jpg', '18', 13, 'Y', '2024-08-30 00:00:00', '2024-08-30 09:26:51', NULL, NULL);
